    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d628">

                <pb facs="0706" n="696" xml:id="pg696"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.203/220: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-02-04T19:00:00-04:00">February 4 [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">10</hi>], 1943—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>210. Your 169, January 30. Department agrees to suggested amendment. Department
                    has no objection to either form of additional paragraph concerning reciprocity
                    but prefers shorter form.</p>
                <p>You are authorized to exchange notes on basis of this telegram and Department’s
                    No. 18, January 4, as soon as the Treaty of January 11<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d628-f1"/> becomes effective.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d628-f1" n="7" xml:id="d628-f1-content">
                <p>Signed at Washington; it provided for relinquishment of extraterritorial rights
                    in China and the regulation of related matters, 57 Stat. 767.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
